{"name":"Brown Sugar","hex":"#ab764e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brown sugar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Sugar which has been only partially refined and still contains molasses.","Refined sugar to which molasses has been added."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown_sugar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brown Sugar (1922 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Brown Sugar is a 1922 British silent romance film directed by Fred Paul and starring Owen Nares, Lillian Hall-Davis and Eric Lewis. It was based on a play by Lady Arthur Lever."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown_Sugar_(1922_film)","wikidata":"Q4976279"},{"title":"Brown Sugar (1931 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Brown Sugar is a 1931 British comedy romance film directed by Leslie S. Hiscott and starring Constance Carpenter, Francis Lister, Allan Aynesworth and Helen Haye. It was written by Cyril Twyford based on the play of the same title by Lady Arthur Lever, and produced by Julius Hagen as a quota quickie for distribution by the American company Warner Brothers."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fa/Brown_Sugar_film_Theatrical_release_poster_%281931%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown_Sugar_(1931_film)","wikidata":"Q4976280"},{"title":"Brown sugar","blocks":[{"text":"Brown sugar is a sucrose sugar product with a distinctive brown color due to the presence of molasses. It is either an unrefined or partially refined soft sugar consisting of sugar crystals with some residual molasses content, or produced by the addition of molasses to refined white sugar. Brown sugar is 98% carbohydrates, containing no dietary fiber or fat, and negligible protein and micronutrient content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Sucre_blanc_cassonade_complet_rapadura.jpg/330px-Sucre_blanc_cassonade_complet_rapadura.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown_sugar","wikidata":"Q11190742"},{"title":"Sugar","blocks":[{"text":"Sugar is a class of sweet-tasting, soluble carbohydrates, many of which are used in food. Simple sugars, also called monosaccharides, include glucose, fructose and galactose. Compound sugars, also called disaccharides or double sugars, are molecules made of two bonded monosaccharides; common examples are sucrose, lactose and maltose. White sugar is almost pure sucrose. During digestion, compound sugars are hydrolysed into simple sugars."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Sucre_blanc_cassonade_complet_rapadura.jpg/330px-Sucre_blanc_cassonade_complet_rapadura.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sugar","wikidata":"Q11002"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Brown_sugar_crystals.JPG/500px-Brown_sugar_crystals.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Brown_sugar_crystals.JPG/1280px-Brown_sugar_crystals.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Brown_sugar_crystals.JPG/500px-Brown_sugar_crystals.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Brown sugar crystals","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrown_sugar_crystals.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Brown_sugar_bricks_%2863%29.jpg/500px-Brown_sugar_bricks_%2863%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Brown_sugar_bricks_%2863%29.jpg/1280px-Brown_sugar_bricks_%2863%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","s